1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,362
Williams Obstetrics.

2
00:00:02,312 --> 00:00:05,425
Chapter 12: Ectopic Pregnancy.

3
00:00:05,425 --> 00:00:27,012
Tubal Pregnancy Tubal Pregnancy Diagnosis Medical Management Surgical Management Interstitial Pregnancy Cesarean Scar Pregnancy Cervical Pregnancy Abdominal Pregnancy Ovarian Pregnancy Heterotopic Pregnancy References Following fertilization and fallopian tube transit, the blastocyst normally implants in the endometrial lining of the uterine cavity.

4
00:00:27,012 --> 00:00:30,575
Implantation elsewhere is considered ectopic.

5
00:00:30,575 --> 00:00:43,600
In the United States, numbers from an insurance database and from Medicaid claims showed ectopic pregnancy rates of 1.54 percent and 1.38 percent, respectively, in 2013 .

6
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:49,025
Ectopic implantation accounts for 3 percent of all pregnancy-related deaths .

7
00:00:49,025 --> 00:01:02,137
Fortunately, beta-human chorionic gonadotropin (β-hCG) assays and transvaginal sonography (TVS) aid earlier diagnosis, maternal survival, and fertility conservation.

8
00:01:02,137 --> 00:01:04,175
Tubal Pregnancy.

9
00:01:04,175 --> 00:01:06,625
# Classification.

10
00:01:06,625 --> 00:01:16,362
Of ectopic pregnancies, nearly 95 percent implant in the fallopian tube’s various segments (Fig. 2-13, p. 26).

11
00:01:16,362 --> 00:01:20,537
The ampulla (70 percent) is the most frequent site .

12
00:01:20,537 --> 00:01:28,037
The rate for isthmic implantation is 12 percent; fimbrial, 11 percent; and interstitial, 2 percent .

13
00:01:28,037 --> 00:01:38,000
Nontubal ectopic pregnancies compose the remaining 5 percent and implant in the ovary, peritoneal cavity, cervix, or prior cesarean scar.

14
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:46,512
Occasionally, a multifetal pregnancy contains one conceptus with normal uterine implantation and the other implanted ectopically.

15
00:01:46,512 --> 00:01:51,062
This is termed a heterotopic pregnancy (p. 231).

16
00:01:51,062 --> 00:01:53,262
Figure 12-1.

17
00:01:53,262 --> 00:01:58,137
Ampullary tubal pregnancy (arrow) seen during laparoscopy.

18
00:01:58,137 --> 00:02:01,787
Reproduced with permission from Dr. Lisa Chao.

19
00:02:01,787 --> 00:02:16,475
For all ectopic pregnancy sites, management is influenced by pregnancy viability, gestational age, maternal health, desires for the index pregnancy and for future fertility, physician skill, and available resources.

20
00:02:16,475 --> 00:02:23,662
Regardless of location, D-negative women with an ectopic pregnancy are given anti-D immunoglobulin.

21
00:02:23,662 --> 00:02:31,512
In first-trimester pregnancies, a single intramuscular 50- or 120-μg dose is appropriate.

22
00:02:31,512 --> 00:02:35,337
Later gestations are given 300 μg .

23
00:02:35,337 --> 00:02:37,412
# Risks.

24
00:02:37,412 --> 00:02:43,312
Abnormal fallopian tube anatomy underlies most cases of tubal ectopic pregnancy.

25
00:02:43,312 --> 00:02:51,225
Surgeries for a prior tubal pregnancy, for fertility restoration, or for sterilization confer the highest risk.

26
00:02:51,225 --> 00:02:58,637
After one prior ectopic pregnancy, the chance of another nears 10 percent (de Bennetot, 2012).

27
00:02:58,637 --> 00:03:04,375
Previous tubal infection, which can distort normal tubal anatomy, is another risk.

28
00:03:04,375 --> 00:03:12,350
Specifically, one episode of salpingitis can be followed by a subsequent ectopic pregnancy in up to 9 percent of women .

29
00:03:12,350 --> 00:03:19,725
Peritubal adhesions that form from salpingitis, appendicitis, or endometriosis also raise chances.

30
00:03:19,725 --> 00:03:32,112
Infertility and the use of assisted reproductive technologies (ART) to overcome it are linked to increased ectopic pregnancy rates (Li, 2015; Perkins, 2015).

31
00:03:32,112 --> 00:03:39,587
Newer techniques aim to lower this rate with ART (Londra, 2015; Zhang, 2017).

32
00:03:39,587 --> 00:03:45,325
Smoking is another known association, although the underlying mechanism is unclear .

33
00:03:45,325 --> 00:03:53,900
Last, with any form of contraception, the absolute number of ectopic pregnancies declines because pregnancy is effectively prevented.

34
00:03:53,900 --> 00:04:02,425
However, some methods more efficiently prevent intracavity implantation and with their failure, ectopic implantation is favored.

35
00:04:02,425 --> 00:04:10,350
These methods are tubal sterilization, intrauterine devices (IUDs), and progestin-only contraceptives.

36
00:04:10,350 --> 00:04:14,187
# Pathogenesis and Potential Outcomes.

37
00:04:14,187 --> 00:04:22,725
With tubal pregnancy, because the fallopian tube lacks a submucosal layer, the fertilized ovum promptly burrows through the epithelium.

38
00:04:22,725 --> 00:04:30,087
The zygote comes to lie near or within the muscularis, which is invaded by rapidly proliferating trophoblast.

39
00:04:30,087 --> 00:04:37,187
Potential outcomes from this include tubal rupture, tubal abortion, or pregnancy failure with resolution.

40
00:04:37,187 --> 00:04:42,600
With rupture, the invading and expanding conceptus can tear the fallopian tube.

41
00:04:42,600 --> 00:04:51,037
Tubal ectopic pregnancies usually rupture spontaneously but may occasionally burst following coitus or bimanual examination.

42
00:04:51,037 --> 00:04:55,000
Hemorrhage usually persists and can become life threatening.

43
00:04:55,000 --> 00:05:00,537
Tubal abortion describes the pregnancy’s passage out the fallopian tube’s distal end.

44
00:05:00,700 --> 00:05:05,712
Subsequently, hemorrhage may cease, and symptoms eventually disappear.

45
00:05:05,662 --> 00:05:11,925
However, bleeding instead can progress to induce symptoms as long as products remain in the tube.

46
00:05:11,925 --> 00:05:19,062
Blood slowly issues from the tubal fimbria into the peritoneal cavity and pools in the rectouterine culde-sac.

47
00:05:19,062 --> 00:05:26,800
If the fimbriated extremity is occluded, the fallopian tube may gradually distend with blood to form a hematosalpinx.

48
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:35,512
Rarely, an aborted fetus will secondarily implant on a peritoneal surface and become an abdominal pregnancy (p. 231).

49
00:05:35,512 --> 00:05:41,812
Last, spontaneous failure reflects ectopic pregnancy death and subsequent reabsorption.

50
00:05:41,812 --> 00:05:48,325
These are now more regularly identified by current sensitive β-hCG assays and surveillance.

51
00:05:48,325 --> 00:05:55,900
Distinctions between acute ectopic pregnancy, just described, and chronic ectopic pregnancy also can be drawn.

52
00:05:55,900 --> 00:06:05,337
Acute ectopic pregnancies are more common, produce a high serum β-hCG level, and grow rapidly, leading to a timely diagnosis.

53
00:06:05,337 --> 00:06:08,350
These carry a greater risk of rupture .

54
00:06:08,350 --> 00:06:17,725
With chronic ectopic pregnancy, abnormal trophoblasts die early, and thus serum β-hCG levels are negative or are low and static.

55
00:06:17,725 --> 00:06:25,337
Chronic ectopic pregnancies typically rupture late, if at all, but commonly form a persistent complex pelvic mass.

56
00:06:25,337 --> 00:06:32,475
This sonographic finding, rather than patient symptoms, often is the reason that prompts diagnostic surgery .

57
00:06:32,475 --> 00:06:35,562
# Clinical Manifestations.

58
00:06:35,562 --> 00:06:39,787
Sources of abdominal pain during pregnancy are extensive.

59
00:06:39,787 --> 00:06:47,775
Uterine conditions include miscarriage, infection, degenerating or enlarging leiomyomas, or round-ligament pain.

60
00:06:47,775 --> 00:06:55,162
Adnexal pain may reflect ectopic pregnancy or ovarian masses that are hemorrhagic, ruptured, or torsed.

61
00:06:55,162 --> 00:07:04,825
Appendicitis, renal stone, cystitis, and gastroenteritis are some nongynecological reasons for lower abdominal pain in early pregnancy.

62
00:07:04,825 --> 00:07:12,812
Thus, an initial urine β-hCG assay, urinalysis, and measure of hemoglobin or hematocrit are routine.

63
00:07:12,812 --> 00:07:21,462
A complete blood count (CBC) to assess the white blood cell count may be preferred if serious infection is a possible diagnosis.

64
00:07:21,462 --> 00:07:28,562
A positive urine pregnancy test result should prompt a serum βhCG assay for those with pain or bleeding.

65
00:07:28,562 --> 00:07:34,562
Before rupture, symptoms and signs of ectopic pregnancy are often subtle or absent.

66
00:07:34,562 --> 00:07:39,625
The classic triad is amenorrhea that is followed by pain and vaginal bleeding.

67
00:07:39,625 --> 00:07:48,025
With tubal rupture, lower abdominal and pelvic pain is usually severe and frequently described as sharp, stabbing, or tearing.

68
00:07:48,025 --> 00:07:53,850
Some degree of vaginal spotting or bleeding is reported by most women with tubal pregnancy.

69
00:07:53,850 --> 00:08:01,737
Although profuse vaginal bleeding suggests an incomplete abortion, such bleeding occasionally is seen with tubal gestations.

70
00:08:01,737 --> 00:08:07,275
Moreover, tubal pregnancy can lead to significant intraabdominal hemorrhage.

71
00:08:07,275 --> 00:08:15,975
Neck or shoulder pain, especially on inspiration, develops in women with diaphragmatic irritation from a sizable hemoperitoneum.

72
00:08:15,975 --> 00:08:20,625
Vertigo and syncope may reflect hemorrhage-related hypovolemia.

73
00:08:20,625 --> 00:08:25,275
Of physical findings, abdominal palpation elicits tenderness.

74
00:08:25,275 --> 00:08:34,612
Bimanual pelvic examination may reveal a mass and tenderness, but this examination should be limited and gentle to avoid iatrogenic rupture.

75
00:08:34,612 --> 00:08:39,550
The uterus itself can be slightly enlarged due to hormonal stimulation.

76
00:08:39,550 --> 00:08:49,850
Responses to moderate bleeding include no change in vital signs, a slight rise in blood pressure, or a vasovagal response with bradycardia and hypotension.

77
00:08:49,850 --> 00:08:56,662
Blood pressure will fall and pulse will rise only if bleeding continues and hypovolemia becomes significant.

78
00:08:56,662 --> 00:09:05,525
Of laboratory findings, hemoglobin or hematocrit readings may at first show only a slight reduction, even after substantive hemorrhage.

79
00:09:05,525 --> 00:09:15,675
Thus, after acute hemorrhage, a trending decline in hemoglobin or hematocrit levels over several hours is a more valuable index of blood loss than is the initial level.

80
00:09:15,675 --> 00:09:25,437
In approximately half of women with a ruptured ectopic pregnancy, varying degrees of leukocytosis may reach 30,000/μL.

81
00:09:25,437 --> 00:09:30,162
Decidua is endometrium that is hormonally prepared for pregnancy.

82
00:09:30,162 --> 00:09:35,325
The degree to which the endometrium is converted with ectopic pregnancy varies.

83
00:09:35,325 --> 00:09:41,575
Thus, in addition to bleeding, women with ectopic tubal pregnancy may pass a decidual cast.

84
00:09:41,575 --> 00:09:43,225
This is

85
00:09:43,396 --> 00:09:48,608
the entire sloughed endometrium that takes the form of the endometrial cavity .

86
00:09:48,558 --> 00:09:53,183
Importantly, decidual sloughing may also occur with miscarriage.

87
00:09:53,183 --> 00:10:01,308
Thus, tissue is carefully examined by the provider and then submitted to evaluate for histological evidence of a conceptus.

88
00:10:01,308 --> 00:10:11,458
If no clear gestational sac is seen by inspection or if no villi are identified histologically, the possibility of ectopic pregnancy must still be considered.

89
00:10:11,458 --> 00:10:13,671
Figure 12-2.

90
00:10:13,671 --> 00:10:19,971
This 7-cm decidual cast was passed by a patient with a tubal ectopic pregnancy.

91
00:10:19,971 --> 00:10:27,496
The cast mirrors the shape of the endometrial cavity, and each arrow marks the portion of decidua that lined the cornua.

92
00:10:27,496 --> 00:10:30,221
Tubal Pregnancy Diagnosis.

93
00:10:30,221 --> 00:10:40,608
For ectopic pregnancy, physical findings, serum β-hCG level measurement, TVS, and at times diagnostic surgery are tools for diagnosis.

94
00:10:40,608 --> 00:10:44,946
Women with evidence of tubal rupture undergo prompt surgery.

95
00:10:44,946 --> 00:10:55,108
For all other hemodynamically stable women without a clearly identified pregnancy, diagnostic strategies use these tools to identify ectopic pregnancy.

96
00:10:55,108 --> 00:10:57,821
Strategies involve trade-offs.

97
00:10:57,821 --> 00:11:05,008
Those that maximize ectopic pregnancy detection may terminate a normal intrauterine pregnancy (IUP).

98
00:11:05,008 --> 00:11:12,696
Conversely, those that reduce the potential interruption of a normal IUP can delay ectopic pregnancy diagnosis.

99
00:11:12,696 --> 00:11:17,921
Patient desires for the index pregnancy are sought and influence these trade-offs.

100
00:11:17,921 --> 00:11:21,571
# Beta-Human Chorionic Gonadotropin.

101
00:11:21,571 --> 00:11:26,458
Rapid and accurate determination of pregnancy is a fundamental step.

102
00:11:26,458 --> 00:11:33,771
hCG is a glycoprotein produced by placental trophoblast and can be detected in serum in early pregnancy.

103
00:11:33,771 --> 00:11:39,408
Current pregnancy tests are immunoassays that seek the beta subunit of hCG.

104
00:11:39,408 --> 00:11:48,083
Lower limits of detection are 20 to 25 mIU/mL for urine and ≤5 mIU/mL for serum .

105
00:11:48,083 --> 00:11:52,571
Different assays can have results that vary by 5 to 10 percent.

106
00:11:52,571 --> 00:11:57,846
Thus, serial values are more reliable when performed by the same laboratory .

107
00:11:57,846 --> 00:12:06,458
For women with a positive pregnancy test result plus bleeding or pain, an initial TVS is typically performed to locate the gestation.

108
00:12:06,458 --> 00:12:12,508
The initial β-hCG level sets expectations for anticipated TVS finding.

109
00:12:12,508 --> 00:12:19,483
With values above a discriminatory threshold, a normal IUP is expected to be seen within the uterus.

110
00:12:19,483 --> 00:12:31,496
Some institutions set their discriminatory threshold at ≥1500 mIU/mL, whereas others use ≥2000 mIU/mL.

111
00:12:31,496 --> 00:12:37,283
Connolly and associates (2013) suggested an even higher threshold.

112
00:12:37,283 --> 00:12:48,571
They noted that with live IUPs, a gestational sac was seen 99 percent of the time in those with a discriminatory level >3510 mIU/mL.

113
00:12:48,571 --> 00:12:51,646
# Transvaginal Sonography.

114
00:12:51,646 --> 00:13:00,833
Pregnancy of Unknown Location If a yolk sac, embryo, or fetus is found within the uterus or within the adnexa, a diagnosis is made.

115
00:13:00,833 --> 00:13:09,396
However, if no evidence of an IUP is seen with TVS, the diagnosis is a pregnancy of unknown location (PUL).

116
00:13:09,396 --> 00:13:20,071
Most PULs reflect: (1) a failing IUP, (2) recent completed abortion, (3) early IUP, or (4) ectopic pregnancy.

117
00:13:20,071 --> 00:13:30,408
Without clear evidence for ectopic pregnancy, serial β-hCG level assessment is reasonable, and a second level is obtained 48 hours after the first.

118
00:13:30,408 --> 00:13:37,246
This practice averts unnecessary methotrexate therapy and avoids harming an early, normal IUP.

119
00:13:37,246 --> 00:13:46,946
With early, normal IUPs, Barnhart and coworkers (2004b) reported a 53percent minimum rise over 48 hours.

120
00:13:46,946 --> 00:13:55,183
Seeber and colleagues (2006) found an even more conservative minimal 35-percent rise in normal IUPs.

121
00:13:55,183 --> 00:14:00,533
With multifetal gestation, this same anticipated rate of rise is expected .

122
00:14:00,533 --> 00:14:13,471
With a PUL ultimately diagnosed as a failed IUP, a pattern of β-hCG level decline also can be anticipated, and levels drop rapidly (Table 11-1, p. 202) .

123
00:14:13,471 --> 00:14:18,296
Sometimes, PULs fail before their location is identified.

124
00:14:18,296 --> 00:14:36,508
With failing PULs, Butts and coworkers (2013) found rates of decline that ranged from 35 to 50 percent at 48 hours and 66 to 87 percent at 7 days for starting hCG values between 250 and 5000 mIU/mL.

125
00:14:36,508 --> 00:14:44,483
Despite these benchmarks, a third of women with an ectopic pregnancy can also have a 53-percent rise at 48 hours .

126
00:14:44,483 --> 00:14:53,321
Overall, approximately half of ectopic pregnancies show declining β-hCG levels, whereas the other half have rising levels.

127
00:14:53,321 --> 00:14:58,921
Importantly, despite a declining βhCG level, a resolving ectopic

128
00:14:59,092 --> 00:15:01,329
pregnancy may rupture.

129
00:15:01,279 --> 00:15:09,092
Rupture at low values likely reflects partial disruption of the vascular connection between trophoblast and maternal vessels.

130
00:15:09,092 --> 00:15:15,592
Here, although β-hCG is produced, it is unable to enter circulation and be detected.

131
00:15:15,592 --> 00:15:23,554
After the initial two β-hCG tests during PUL assessment, additional levels are drawn every 2 to 7 days.

132
00:15:23,554 --> 00:15:31,979
In general, testing is typically more frequent if symptoms or β-hCG level trends reflect a higher ectopic pregnancy risk .

133
00:15:31,979 --> 00:15:34,804
TVS also may be repeated.

134
00:15:34,804 --> 00:15:41,967
This serial assessment to reach a diagnosis is balanced against the rupture risk if the pregnancy is indeed ectopic.

135
00:15:41,967 --> 00:15:46,229
Dilation and curettage (D & C) is an option .

136
00:15:46,229 --> 00:15:50,942
It may give a faster diagnosis but may interrupt a normal IUP.

137
00:15:50,942 --> 00:15:58,279
Before curettage, a second TVS examination may be indicated and may display new informative findings.

138
00:15:58,279 --> 00:16:03,867
As noted, ectopic pregnancies can rupture even at low β-hCG levels.

139
00:16:03,867 --> 00:16:11,629
Thus, serum β-hCG values are usually followed until they lie below the negative-result threshold for the given assay.

140
00:16:11,629 --> 00:16:22,029
Endometrial Findings In a woman in whom ectopic pregnancy is suspected, TVS is performed to look for findings indicative of an IUP or ectopic pregnancy.

141
00:16:22,029 --> 00:16:30,892
During endometrial cavity evaluation, an intrauterine gestational sac is usually visible between 4½ and 5 weeks.

142
00:16:30,892 --> 00:16:42,942
The yolk sac appears between 5 and 6 weeks, and a fetal pole with cardiac activity is first detected at 5½ to 6 weeks (Fig. 14-1, p. 248).

143
00:16:42,942 --> 00:16:48,292
With transabdominal sonography, these structures are visualized slightly later.

144
00:16:48,292 --> 00:16:54,892
In contrast, with ectopic pregnancy, a trilaminar endometrial pattern is characteristic .

145
00:16:54,892 --> 00:17:00,904
Its specificity is 94 percent, but with a sensitivity of only 38 percent .

146
00:17:00,904 --> 00:17:14,342
In addition, Moschos and Twickler (2008) determined in women with a PUL at presentation that no normal IUPs had an endometrial stripe thickness <8 mm. Figure 12-3.

147
00:17:14,342 --> 00:17:20,129
Transvaginal sonography of a pseudogestational sac within the endometrial cavity.

148
00:17:20,129 --> 00:17:25,367
Its central location is characteristic of these anechoic fluid collections.

149
00:17:25,367 --> 00:17:33,242
The endometrium is marked by calipers, and distal to this fluid, the endometrial thickness has a trilaminar pattern.

150
00:17:33,242 --> 00:17:36,742
This pattern is common with ectopic pregnancy.

151
00:17:36,742 --> 00:17:41,117
Reproduced with permission from Jason McWhirt, ARDMS.

152
00:17:41,117 --> 00:17:50,329
Anechoic fluid collections, which might normally suggest an early intrauterine gestational sac, may also be seen with ectopic pregnancy.

153
00:17:50,329 --> 00:17:54,467
These include pseudogestational sac and decidual cyst.

154
00:17:54,467 --> 00:18:03,279
First, a pseudosac is a fluid collection between the endometrial layers and conforms to the cavity shape (see Fig. 12-3).

155
00:18:03,279 --> 00:18:08,192
If a pseudosac is noted, the risk of ectopic pregnancy is increased .

156
00:18:08,192 --> 00:18:18,729
Second, a decidual cyst is identified as an anechoic area lying within the endometrium but remote from the canal and often at the endometrial–myometrial border.

157
00:18:18,729 --> 00:18:23,767
This may represent early decidual breakdown that precedes cast formation .

158
00:18:23,767 --> 00:18:29,079
These two findings contrast with the intradecidual sign seen with IUPs.

159
00:18:29,079 --> 00:18:37,404
With this sign, the early gestational sac is an anechoic sac eccentrically located within one of the endometrial stripe layers .

160
00:18:37,404 --> 00:18:48,404
The American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists (2020) advises caution in diagnosing an IUP if a definite yolk sac or embryo is not seen.

161
00:18:48,404 --> 00:18:56,454
Adnexal Findings The sonographic diagnosis of ectopic pregnancy rests on seeing an adnexal mass separate from the ovary .

162
00:18:56,454 --> 00:19:04,004
If an extrauterine yolk sac, embryo, or fetus is identified, ectopic pregnancy is clearly confirmed.

163
00:19:04,004 --> 00:19:11,192
In other cases, a hyperechoic halo or tubal ring surrounding an anechoic gestational sac is seen.

164
00:19:11,192 --> 00:19:18,004
Alternatively, hemorrhage within the ectopic pregnancy can form a solid, complex adnexal mass.

165
00:19:18,004 --> 00:19:30,429
Overall, 60 percent of ectopic pregnancies are a complex mass; 20 percent are a hyperechoic ring; and 13 percent have an obvious gestational sac with a yolk sac or embryo .

166
00:19:30,429 --> 00:19:35,792
Importantly, not all adnexal masses represent an ectopic pregnancy.

167
00:19:35,792 --> 00:19:42,317
In this case, integration of sonographic findings with other clinical information is necessary.

168
00:19:42,317 --> 00:19:44,642
Figure 12-4.

169
00:19:44,642 --> 00:19:50,104
Various transvaginal sonographic findings with ectopic tubal pregnancies.

170
00:19:50,104 --> 00:19:55,404
For sonographic diagnosis, an ectopic mass should be seen in the adnexa

171
00:19:55,564 --> 00:20:13,026
separate from the ovary and may be seen as: (A) a yolk sac (shown here) and/or fetal pole with or without cardiac activity within an extrauterine sac, (B) an empty extrauterine sac with a hyperechoic ring, or (C) an inhomogeneous adnexal mass.

172
00:20:13,026 --> 00:20:21,976
In this last image, color Doppler shows a classic “ring of fire,” which reflects increased vascularity typical of ectopic pregnancies.

173
00:20:21,976 --> 00:20:29,839
LT OV = left ovary; SAG LT AD = sagittal left adnexal; UT = uterus.

174
00:20:29,839 --> 00:20:38,514
Placental blood flow within the periphery of the complex adnexal mass —the ring of fire—can be seen with application of color Doppler.

175
00:20:38,514 --> 00:20:45,576
A corpus luteum cyst often displays a similar vascular pattern, and differentiation can be challenging.

176
00:20:45,576 --> 00:20:53,039
Hemoperitoneum In affected women, blood in the peritoneal cavity is most often identified using TVS .

177
00:20:53,039 --> 00:20:57,389
A small amount of peritoneal fluid is physiologically normal.

178
00:20:57,389 --> 00:21:05,464
However, with hemoperitoneum, anechoic or hypoechoic fluid initially collects in the dependent retrouterine cul-de-sac.

179
00:21:05,464 --> 00:21:09,926
It then additionally surrounds the uterus as blood fills the pelvis.

180
00:21:09,926 --> 00:21:17,514
With significant intraabdominal hemorrhage, blood will track up the pericolic gutters to fill Morison pouch near the liver.

181
00:21:17,514 --> 00:21:29,201
Free fluid in this pouch typically is not seen until accumulated volumes reach 400 to 600 mL (Branney, 1995; Rodgerson, 2001).

182
00:21:29,201 --> 00:21:38,889
Diagnostically, peritoneal fluid in conjunction with an adnexal mass and a positive pregnancy test result are highly predictive of ectopic pregnancy .

183
00:21:38,889 --> 00:21:42,139
Ascites from cancer is a notable mimic.

184
00:21:42,139 --> 00:21:44,539
Figure 12-5.

185
00:21:44,539 --> 00:21:46,489
Hemoperitoneum.

186
00:21:46,489 --> 00:21:54,501
A. This transvaginal sagittal view of the pelvis shows anechoic fluid initially pooling in the retrouterine cul-de-sac ().

187
00:21:54,501 --> 00:21:59,326
Large accumulations will also extend into the anterior cul-de-sac ().

188
00:21:59,326 --> 00:22:05,989
B. In this right upper quadrant sonogram, anechoic fluid is seen in Morison pouch (arrowhead).

189
00:22:05,989 --> 00:22:11,989
C = cervix; F = fundus; K = kidney; L = liver.

190
00:22:11,989 --> 00:22:15,839
Reproduced with permission from Dr. Devin Macias.

191
00:22:15,839 --> 00:22:22,564
If sonography is unavailable, culdocentesis is a simple technique and was used commonly in the past.

192
00:22:22,564 --> 00:22:34,164
The cervix is pulled outward and upward toward the symphysis with a tenaculum, and a long, 18-gauge needle is inserted through the posterior vaginal fornix into the retrouterine cul-de-sac.

193
00:22:34,164 --> 00:22:37,301
If present, fluid can be aspirated.

194
00:22:37,301 --> 00:22:43,476
However, no fluid is interpreted only as unsatisfactory entry into the cul-de-sac.

195
00:22:43,476 --> 00:22:48,464
Bloody fluid or fluid with old clot fragments suggests hemoperitoneum.

196
00:22:48,464 --> 00:22:56,101
If the blood sample clots, it may reflect an adjacent blood vessel puncture or brisk bleeding from ectopic pregnancy rupture.

197
00:22:56,101 --> 00:22:58,814
# Serum Progesterone.

198
00:22:58,814 --> 00:23:09,226
Although not our practice, this hormone is used by some to aid ectopic pregnancy diagnosis when serum β-hCG levels and TVS findings are inconclusive .

199
00:23:09,226 --> 00:23:11,826
A single value is sufficient.

200
00:23:11,826 --> 00:23:25,564
From studies, a serum progesterone level <6 ng/mL (<20 nmol/L) has a pooled specificity of 98 percent to predict a nonviable pregnancy in women with a PUL .

201
00:23:25,564 --> 00:23:35,364
A value >25 ng/mL suggests a live IUP and excludes ectopic pregnancy with 97-percent sensitivity .

202
00:23:35,364 --> 00:23:44,976
With most ectopic pregnancies, progesterone levels range between 10 and 25 ng/mL and thus have limited diagnostic utility .

203
00:23:44,976 --> 00:23:52,801
Serum progesterone levels can be used to buttress a clinical impression, but again they cannot reliably identify location .

204
00:23:52,801 --> 00:23:55,664
# Endometrial Sampling.

205
00:23:55,664 --> 00:24:02,864
Several endometrial changes accompany ectopic pregnancy, and all lack coexistent chorionic villi.

206
00:24:02,864 --> 00:24:12,839
Decidual reaction is found in 42 percent of samples, secretory endometrium in 22 percent, and proliferative endometrium in 12 percent .

207
00:24:12,839 --> 00:24:19,901
Some recommend that lack of chorionic villi be confirmed by D & C before methotrexate treatment is given.

208
00:24:19,901 --> 00:24:32,614
Chung and associates (2011) found that the presumptive diagnosis of ectopic pregnancy is inaccurate in 27 percent of cases without histological exclusion of a spontaneous pregnancy loss.

209
00:24:32,614 --> 00:24:39,189
Nevertheless, the risks of D & C are weighed against the limited maternal risks of methotrexate.

210
00:24:39,189 --> 00:24:53,151
Endometrial biopsy with a Pipelle catheter or endometrial aspiration was studied as an alternative to surgical curettage and found inferior (Barnhart, 2003b; Insogna, 2017).

211
00:24:53,151 --> 00:24:55,951
Instead, frozen section of

212
00:24:56,116 --> 00:25:02,966
curettage fragments to identify products of conception is accurate in 95 percent of cases .

213
00:25:02,916 --> 00:25:05,391
# Laparoscopy.

214
00:25:05,391 --> 00:25:15,203
Direct visualization of the fallopian tubes and pelvis by laparoscopy offers a reliable diagnosis in most cases of suspected ectopic pregnancy.

215
00:25:15,203 --> 00:25:21,828
This also permits a ready transition to definitive operative therapy, which is discussed subsequently.

216
00:25:21,828 --> 00:25:23,941
Medical Management.

217
00:25:23,941 --> 00:25:26,516
# Regimen Options.

218
00:25:26,516 --> 00:25:33,616
For most ectopic pregnancies, medical therapy is preferred, if feasible, to avoid surgical risks.

219
00:25:33,616 --> 00:25:39,328
Disqualifying criteria are a ruptured fallopian tube and drug contraindications.

220
00:25:39,328 --> 00:25:47,016
Other considerations include reasonably close access to emergency care and a commitment to surveillance laboratory testing.

221
00:25:47,016 --> 00:25:52,928
Medical therapy traditionally involves the antimetabolite methotrexate (MTX).

222
00:25:52,928 --> 00:25:56,266
This drug is a folic acid antagonist.

223
00:25:56,266 --> 00:26:05,941
It tightly binds to dihydrofolate reductase, blocking the reduction of dihydrofolate to tetrahydrofolate, which is the active form of folic acid.

224
00:26:05,941 --> 00:26:14,866
As a result, de novo purine and pyrimidine production is halted, which then arrests DNA, RNA, and protein synthesis.

225
00:26:14,866 --> 00:26:20,466
Thus, MTX is highly effective against rapidly proliferating trophoblast.

226
00:26:20,466 --> 00:26:27,628
However, gastrointestinal mucosa, bone marrow, and respiratory epithelium also can be harmed.

227
00:26:27,628 --> 00:26:32,453
To help select suitable candidates, laboratory tests are obtained.

228
00:26:32,453 --> 00:26:42,278
First, MTX is renally cleared, and significant renal dysfunction, reflected by an elevated serum creatinine level, precludes its use.

229
00:26:42,278 --> 00:26:51,603
Second, MTX can be hepato- and myelotoxic, and CBC and liver function tests (LFTs) help establish a baseline.

230
00:26:51,603 --> 00:26:55,653
Last, blood type and Rh status are determined.

231
00:26:55,653 --> 00:27:03,453
All except blood typing are considered surveillance laboratory tests and are repeated prior to additional MTX doses.

232
00:27:03,453 --> 00:27:10,228
With administration, women are counseled to avoid several aggravating agents until treatment is completed.

233
00:27:10,228 --> 00:27:39,141
These are: (1) folic acid-containing supplements, which can competitively reduce MTX binding to dihydrofolate reductase; (2) nonsteroidal antiinflammatory drugs, which reduce renal blood flow and delay drug excretion; (3) alcohol, which can predispose to concurrent hepatic enzyme elevation; (4) sunlight, which can provoke MTXrelated dermatitis; and (5) sexual activity, which can rupture the ectopic pregnancy .

234
00:27:39,141 --> 00:27:48,641
MTX is a potent teratogen, and MTX embryopathy is notable for craniofacial and skeletal abnormalities and fetal-growth restriction .

235
00:27:48,641 --> 00:28:02,416
MTX is excreted into breast milk and may accumulate in neonatal tissues and interfere with neonatal cellular metabolism (American Academy of Pediatrics, 2001; Briggs, 2017).

236
00:28:02,416 --> 00:28:10,628
Based on all these findings, a list of contraindications and pretherapy laboratory testing is found in Table 12-1.

237
00:28:10,628 --> 00:28:12,866
Table 12-1.

238
00:28:12,866 --> 00:28:27,353
Medical Treatment Protocols for Ectopic Pregnancy For ease and efficacy, intramuscular MTX administration is used most often for ectopic pregnancy treatment, and single-dose and multidose MTX protocols are available.

239
00:28:27,353 --> 00:28:39,416
With single-dose therapy, the dose is 50 mg/m2 body surface area (BSA), and BSA can be derived using various Internet-based BSA calculators.

240
00:28:39,416 --> 00:28:47,153
At our institution, patients are observed for 30 minutes following MTX injection to exclude an adverse reaction.

241
00:28:47,153 --> 00:28:52,703
With the multidose regimen, leucovorin is added to blunt MTX toxicity.

242
00:28:52,703 --> 00:28:57,041
Leucovorin is folinic acid and has folic acid activity.

243
00:28:57,041 --> 00:29:02,441
Thus, it allows some purine and pyrimidine synthesis to buffer side effects.

244
00:29:02,441 --> 00:29:06,678
Comparing these two protocols, trade-offs are recognized.

245
00:29:06,678 --> 00:29:13,441
Single-dose therapy offers simplicity, less expense, and less intensive posttherapy monitoring.

246
00:29:13,441 --> 00:29:25,678
However, some but not all studies report a higher success rate for the multidose regimen (Barnhart, 2003a; Lipscomb, 2005; Tabatabaii, 2012).

247
00:29:25,678 --> 00:29:32,491
Overall, ectopic tubal pregnancy resolution rates approximate 90 percent with MTX use.

248
00:29:32,491 --> 00:29:36,503
At our institution, we use single-dose MTX.

249
00:29:36,503 --> 00:29:39,091
# Patient Selection.

250
00:29:39,091 --> 00:29:45,653
The best candidate for medical therapy is the woman who is asymptomatic, motivated, and compliant.

251
00:29:45,653 --> 00:29:57,391
With medical therapy, some classic predictors of success include a low initial serum β-hCG level, small ectopic pregnancy size, and absent fetal cardiac activity.

252
00:29:57,391 --> 00:30:01,178
Of these, initial serum β-hCG level

253
00:30:01,348 --> 00:30:05,773
is the best prognostic indicator with single-dose MTX.

254
00:30:05,723 --> 00:30:28,385
Reported failure rates are 1.5 percent if the initial serum β-hCG concentration is <1000 mIU/mL; 5.6 percent at 1000 to 2000 mIU/mL; 3.8 percent at 2000 to 5000 mIU/mL; and 14.3 percent for levels between 5000 and 10,000 mIU/mL .

255
00:30:28,385 --> 00:30:33,560
Many early trials also used large size as an exclusion criterion.

256
00:30:33,560 --> 00:30:45,285
Lipscomb and colleagues (1998) reported a 93-percent success rate with single-dose MTX when the ectopic mass was ≤3.5 cm.

257
00:30:45,285 --> 00:30:52,873
This compared with success rates between 87 and 90 percent when the mass was >3.5 cm.

258
00:30:52,873 --> 00:31:02,310
These authors also found ectopic pregnancies measuring ≤4 cm and lacking cardiac activity to be suitable candidates.

259
00:31:02,310 --> 00:31:09,548
Failure rates rise if cardiac activity is seen, with an 87-percent success rate in such cases.

260
00:31:09,548 --> 00:31:11,923
# Side Effects.

261
00:31:11,923 --> 00:31:19,410
These regimens are associated with minimal laboratory changes and symptoms, but rarely toxicity may be severe.

262
00:31:19,410 --> 00:31:29,435
Kooi and Kock (1992) reviewed 16 studies and reported that adverse effects were resolved by 3 to 4 days after MTX was discontinued.

263
00:31:29,435 --> 00:31:37,710
The most frequent were liver involvement—12 percent; stomatitis—6 percent; and gastroenteritis—1 percent.

264
00:31:37,710 --> 00:31:40,673
One woman had bone marrow depression.

265
00:31:40,673 --> 00:31:49,435
More commonly, 65 to 75 percent of women given MTX will have increasing pain beginning several days after therapy.

266
00:31:49,435 --> 00:31:57,998
Thought to reflect separation of the ectopic pregnancy from the tubal wall, this pain generally is mild and relieved by analgesics.

267
00:31:57,998 --> 00:32:11,573
In a series of 258 women treated with MTX by Lipscomb and colleagues (1999), 20 percent had pain that merited evaluation in a clinic or emergency department to exclude tubal rupture.

268
00:32:11,573 --> 00:32:16,298
Long term, MTX treatment does not diminish ovarian reserve .

269
00:32:16,298 --> 00:32:27,610
However, after successful MTX therapy, pregnancy is ideally delayed for at least 3 months, because this drug may persist in human tissues for months after a single dose .

270
00:32:27,610 --> 00:32:33,510
Although data are very limited, conception before this waiting period appears reassuring.

271
00:32:33,510 --> 00:32:44,235
In one study, 45 women who conceived <6 months after MTX had similar pregnancy outcomes compared with 80 women who conceived >6 months after MTX .

272
00:32:44,235 --> 00:32:46,535
# Surveillance.

273
00:32:46,535 --> 00:32:58,573
As shown in Table 12-1, monitoring single-dose therapy calls for serum βhCG determinations at days 4 and 7 following initial MTX injection on day 1.

274
00:32:58,573 --> 00:33:07,710
After single-dose MTX, mean serum β-hCG levels may rise or fall during the first 4 days and then should gradually decline.

275
00:33:07,710 --> 00:33:16,410
If the level fails to drop by ≥15 percent between days 4 and 7, a second MTX dose is recommended.

276
00:33:16,410 --> 00:33:21,598
This is necessary in 20 percent of women treated with single-dose therapy .

277
00:33:21,598 --> 00:33:27,373
In such cases, a CBC, creatinine level, and LFTs are rechecked.

278
00:33:27,373 --> 00:33:32,610
If these surveillance tests are normal, a second equivalent dose is administered.

279
00:33:32,610 --> 00:33:38,410
The date of this second injection will become the new day 1, and the protocol is restarted.

280
00:33:38,410 --> 00:33:49,573
Multidose therapy provides MTX (1 mg/kg) treatment with leucovorin (0.1 mg/kg) therapy on alternating days.

281
00:33:49,573 --> 00:33:55,660
After this first pair of injections, a serum β-hCG concentration is obtained.

282
00:33:55,660 --> 00:34:02,260
Values between days 1 and 3 are anticipated to drop by ≥15 percent.

283
00:34:02,260 --> 00:34:08,785
If not and if surveillance tests are normal, an additional MTX/leucovorin pair is given.

284
00:34:08,785 --> 00:34:13,060
A serum β-hCG level is repeated 2 days later.

285
00:34:13,060 --> 00:34:16,410
Up to four doses may be given if required .

286
00:34:16,410 --> 00:34:27,773
With either dosing regimen, once a decline ≥15 percent is achieved, weekly serum β-hCG level testing then begins until values are undetectable.

287
00:34:27,773 --> 00:34:44,248
Lipscomb and colleagues (1998) used single-dose MTX to successfully treat 287 women and reported that the average time to resolution—defined as a serum β-hCG level <15 mIU/mL—was 34 days.

288
00:34:44,248 --> 00:34:47,498
The longest time was 109 days.

289
00:34:47,498 --> 00:34:49,685
Surgical Management.

290
00:34:49,685 --> 00:34:51,848
# Options.

291
00:34:51,848 --> 00:34:56,148
Before surgery, future fertility desires are discussed.

292
00:34:56,148 --> 00:35:01,960
In women desiring sterilization, the unaffected tube can be ligated or removed.

293
00:35:01,960 --> 00:35:06,948
This is done concurrently with salpingectomy for the ectopic-containing tube.

294
00:35:06,948 --> 00:35:14,385
Laparoscopy is the preferred surgical approach for ectopic pregnancy unless a woman is hemodynamically unstable.

295
00:35:14,385 --> 00:35:21,623
This is supported first by comparable subsequent uterine pregnancy rates and tubal patency rates in those undergoing

296
00:35:21,772 --> 00:35:26,709
salpingostomy completed either by laparoscopy or by laparotomy .

297
00:35:26,659 --> 00:35:35,397
Second, laparoscopy has lower infection, adhesion, and thromboembolism risks and faster recovery times than laparotomy.

298
00:35:35,397 --> 00:35:48,284
Moreover, as experience has accrued, cases previously managed by laparotomy—for example, those with hemoperitoneum—can safely be managed laparoscopically by those with suitable expertise.

299
00:35:48,284 --> 00:35:59,234
However, the lowered venous return and cardiac output associated with pneumoperitoneum must be factored into the selection of minimally invasive surgery for a hypovolemic woman.

300
00:35:59,234 --> 00:36:04,359
Two procedures—salpingostomy or salpingectomy—are options.

301
00:36:04,359 --> 00:36:09,347
In the past, some favored salpingostomy to preserve future fertility.

302
00:36:09,347 --> 00:36:18,484
However, two randomized trials compared laparoscopic outcomes between the two procedures in women with a normal contralateral fallopian tube.

303
00:36:18,484 --> 00:36:29,272
The European Surgery in Ectopic Pregnancy (ESEP) study randomized 231 women to salpingectomy and 215 to salpingostomy.

304
00:36:29,272 --> 00:36:41,172
After surgery, the subsequent cumulative rates of ongoing pregnancy by natural conception did not differ significantly between groups—56 versus 61 percent, respectively .

305
00:36:41,172 --> 00:36:51,409
Again, in the DEMETER trial, the subsequent 2-year rate for achieving an IUP did not differ between groups—64 versus 70 percent, respectively .

306
00:36:51,409 --> 00:37:01,797
However, for women with an abnormalappearing contralateral tube, salpingostomy of the ectopic-containing tube may be preferred if feasible to help preserve fertility.

307
00:37:01,797 --> 00:37:08,734
Of the two procedures, salpingectomy may be used for both ruptured and unruptured ectopic pregnancies.

308
00:37:08,734 --> 00:37:16,047
With one laparoscopic technique, the affected fallopian tube is lifted and held with atraumatic grasping forceps.

309
00:37:16,047 --> 00:37:23,172
One of several suitable bipolar grasping devices is placed across the fallopian tube at the uterotubal junction.

310
00:37:23,172 --> 00:37:27,597
Once desiccated, the tube is cut from its uterine attachment.

311
00:37:27,597 --> 00:37:33,184
The bipolar device is then advanced across the mesosalpinx to free the entire tube.

312
00:37:33,184 --> 00:37:38,247
Salpingostomy is typically used to remove a small unruptured pregnancy.

313
00:37:38,247 --> 00:37:46,234
A 10- to 15-mm linear incision is made on the antimesenteric border of the fallopian tube and over the pregnancy.

314
00:37:46,234 --> 00:37:49,859
The products usually will extrude from the incision.

315
00:37:49,859 --> 00:37:57,997
These can be carefully extracted or can be flushed out using high-pressure irrigation that more thoroughly removes the trophoblastic tissue.

316
00:37:57,997 --> 00:38:07,234
Small bleeding sites are controlled with needlepoint electrosurgical coagulation, and the incision is left unsutured to heal by secondary intention .

317
00:38:07,234 --> 00:38:17,284
With either procedure and after specimen removal, the pelvis and abdomen are irrigated and suctioned free of blood and tissue debris to remove all trophoblastic tissue.

318
00:38:17,284 --> 00:38:20,222
# Persistent Trophoblast.

319
00:38:20,222 --> 00:38:26,322
After trophoblast removal during surgery, β-hCG levels usually fall quickly.

320
00:38:26,322 --> 00:38:38,084
Persistent trophoblast is rare following salpingectomy but complicates 5 to 15 percent of salpingostomy cases (Pouly, 1986; Seifer, 1993).

321
00:38:38,084 --> 00:38:44,634
Incomplete trophoblast removal can be identified by stable or rising β-hCG levels .

322
00:38:44,634 --> 00:38:47,872
Monitoring approaches are not codified.

323
00:38:47,872 --> 00:38:51,872
Weekly measures are reasonable following salpingostomy .

324
00:38:51,872 --> 00:39:00,634
Following uncomplicated salpingectomy, we do not repeat β-hCG levels in women without pain or symptoms of hemoperitoneum.

325
00:39:00,634 --> 00:39:07,847
With stable or increasing β-hCG levels, additional surgical or medical therapy is necessary.

326
00:39:07,847 --> 00:39:18,547
In those without evidence for tubal rupture, standard therapy for persistent trophoblast is single-dose MTX, 50 mg/m2 × BSA.

327
00:39:18,547 --> 00:39:22,322
Tubal rupture and bleeding require a second surgery.

328
00:39:22,322 --> 00:39:25,759
# Medical versus Surgical Therapy.

329
00:39:25,759 --> 00:39:34,747
Of options, multidose MTX treatment and laparoscopic salpingostomy have been compared in one randomized trial of 100 patients.

330
00:39:34,747 --> 00:39:47,372
The authors found no differences for rates of tubal preservation, primary treatment success, and subsequent fertility (Dias Pereira, 1999; Hajenius, 1997).

331
00:39:47,372 --> 00:39:54,622
For single-dose MTX, its efficacy compared with laparoscopic salpingostomy shows conflicting results.

332
00:39:54,622 --> 00:40:08,609
In one randomized trial, single-dose MTX was less successful in pregnancy resolution, whereas in the other, single-dose MTX was equally effective (Saraj, 1998; Sowter, 2001).

333
00:40:08,609 --> 00:40:13,659
Krag Moeller and associates (2009) reported during a median

334
00:40:13,828 --> 00:40:28,865
surveillance period of 8.6 years that ectopic-resolution success rates and cumulative spontaneous IUP rates were not significantly different between those managed by laparoscopic salpingostomy and those treated with single-dose MTX.

335
00:40:28,815 --> 00:40:34,790
Salpingectomy effectively removes the entire conceptus and yields high resolution rates.

336
00:40:34,790 --> 00:40:38,315
It thus outperforms MTX in this regard.

337
00:40:38,315 --> 00:40:52,128
Yet, when future fertility and ectopic pregnancy recurrence rates are analyzed, both salpingectomy and MTX therapy show comparable results (de Bennetot, 2012; Irani, 2017).

338
00:40:52,128 --> 00:41:01,428
In another study, surgery, MTX, or expectant management all yielded statistically similar subsequent spontaneous IUP rates .

339
00:41:01,428 --> 00:41:16,753
In sum, medical or surgical management offer similar outcomes in women who are hemodynamically stable, have serum β-hCG concentrations <5000 mIU/mL, and have a small pregnancy with no cardiac activity.

340
00:41:16,753 --> 00:41:34,340
Despite lower success rates with medical therapy for women with larger tubal size, higher serum β-hCG levels, and fetal cardiac activity, medical management can be offered to the motivated woman who understands the risks of emergency surgery in the event of treatment failure.

341
00:41:34,340 --> 00:41:37,065
# Expectant Management.

342
00:41:37,065 --> 00:41:47,365
In select asymptomatic women, observation of a very early tubal pregnancy that is associated with stable or falling serum β-hCG levels is reasonable.

343
00:41:47,365 --> 00:41:53,815
A commitment to surveillance visits and relative proximity to emergency care are other safeguards.

344
00:41:53,815 --> 00:41:59,790
Importantly, this differs from expectant management of a PUL during its evaluation.

345
00:41:59,790 --> 00:42:14,815
Predictive factors for success include a low initial serum β-hCG concentration, a significant drop in levels over 48 hours, and a sonographic inhomogeneous mass rather than a tubal halo or other gestational structures.

346
00:42:14,815 --> 00:42:28,515
For example, initial values <175 mIU/mL predict spontaneous resolution in 88 to 96 percent of attempts (Elson, 2004; Kirk, 2011).

347
00:42:28,515 --> 00:42:42,678
Initial values <1000 mIU/mL have success rates ranging from 71 to 92 percent (Jurkovic, 2017; Mavrelos, 2013; Silva, 2015).

348
00:42:42,678 --> 00:42:50,190
With expectant management, subsequent rates of tubal patency and intrauterine pregnancy are comparable with surgery .

349
00:42:50,190 --> 00:43:03,565
That said, compared with the established safety of medical or surgical therapy, the prolonged surveillance and risks of tubal rupture support the practice of expectant therapy only in appropriately selected and counseled women.

350
00:43:03,565 --> 00:43:05,903
Interstitial Pregnancy.

351
00:43:05,903 --> 00:43:08,303
# Diagnosis.

352
00:43:08,303 --> 00:43:15,203
An interstitial pregnancy is one that implants within the tubal segment that lies within the muscular uterine wall .

353
00:43:15,203 --> 00:43:25,065
Incorrectly, they may be called cornual pregnancies, but this term describes a conception that develops in the rudimentary horn of a uterus with a müllerian anomaly.

354
00:43:25,065 --> 00:43:35,528
Risk factors are similar to others discussed for tubal ectopic pregnancy, although previous ipsilateral salpingectomy is a specific one for interstitial pregnancy .

355
00:43:35,528 --> 00:43:44,990
Undiagnosed interstitial pregnancies usually rupture following 8 to 16 weeks of amenorrhea, which is later than for more distal tubal pregnancies.

356
00:43:44,990 --> 00:43:51,790
The myometrium covering the interstitial fallopian tube segment permits greater distention before rupture.

357
00:43:51,790 --> 00:44:02,265
Because of the proximity of these pregnancies to the uterine and ovarian arteries, hemorrhage can be severe and associated with mortality rates as high as 2.5 percent .

358
00:44:02,265 --> 00:44:04,590
Figure 12-6.

359
00:44:04,590 --> 00:44:07,540
Interstitial ectopic pregnancy.

360
00:44:07,540 --> 00:44:18,078
A. This parasagittal view using transvaginal sonography shows an empty uterine cavity and a mass that is cephalad and lateral to the uterine fundus (calipers).

361
00:44:18,078 --> 00:44:25,103
B. Intraoperative photograph during laparotomy and before cornual resection of the same ectopic pregnancy.

362
00:44:25,103 --> 00:44:35,665
In this frontal view, the bulging right-sided interstitial ectopic pregnancy is lateral to the round ligament insertion and medial to the isthmic portion of the fallopian tube.

363
00:44:35,665 --> 00:44:40,590
Reproduced with permission from Drs. David Rogers and Elaine Duryea.

364
00:44:40,590 --> 00:44:47,090
In many cases, these pregnancies are identified early, but diagnosis can still be challenging.

365
00:44:47,090 --> 00:44:55,828
These pregnancies sonographically can appear similar to an eccentrically implanted IUP, especially in a uterus with a müllerian anomaly.

366
00:44:55,828 --> 00:45:00,690
Criteria that may aid differentiation include: an empty uterus,

367
00:45:00,844 --> 00:45:14,281
a gestational sac seen separate from the endometrium and >1 cm away from the most lateral edge of the uterine cavity, and a thin, <5-mm myometrial mantle surrounding the sac .

368
00:45:14,231 --> 00:45:28,844
Moreover, an echogenic line, known as the interstitial line sign, extending from the gestational sac to the endometrial cavity most likely represents the interstitial portion of the fallopian tube and is highly sensitive and specific .

369
00:45:28,844 --> 00:45:39,869
In unclear cases, three-dimensional (3-D) sonography, magnetic resonance (MR) imaging, or diagnostic laparoscopy can help clarify anatomy.

370
00:45:39,869 --> 00:45:48,819
Laparoscopically, a myometrial protuberance is seen to lie lateral to the round ligament and coexists with normal distal tubes and ovaries.

371
00:45:48,819 --> 00:45:51,044
# Management.

372
00:45:51,044 --> 00:46:02,719
Surgically, either cornual resection or cornuostomy may be performed via laparotomy or laparoscopy, depending on patient hemodynamic stability and surgeon expertise.

373
00:46:02,719 --> 00:46:09,769
With either approach, intraoperative intramyometrial vasopressin injection may limit surgical blood loss.

374
00:46:09,769 --> 00:46:16,806
Cornual resection removes the gestational sac and surrounding cornual myometrium by means of a wedge excision .

375
00:46:16,806 --> 00:46:25,094
Alternatively, cornuostomy involves incision of the cornual myometrium and suction or instrument extraction of the pregnancy.

376
00:46:25,094 --> 00:46:29,119
Both instances require layered myometrial closure.

377
00:46:29,119 --> 00:46:34,931
β-hCG levels are monitored postoperatively to exclude remnant trophoblast.

378
00:46:34,931 --> 00:46:37,406
Figure 12-7.

379
00:46:37,406 --> 00:46:45,381
During cornual resection, the pregnancy, surrounding myometrium, and ipsilateral fallopian tube are excised en bloc.

380
00:46:45,381 --> 00:46:48,881
The incision is angled inward as it is deepened.

381
00:46:48,881 --> 00:46:55,606
This creates a wedge shape into the myometrium, which is then closed in layers with delayed-absorbable suture.

382
00:46:55,606 --> 00:46:59,869
The serosa is closed with subcuticular style suturing.

383
00:46:59,869 --> 00:47:08,231
Reproduced with permission from Hoffman BL, Hamid CA, Corton MM: Surgeries for benign gynecologic conditions.

384
00:47:08,231 --> 00:47:15,456
In Hoffman BL, Schorge JO, Halvorson LM, et al: Williams Gynecology, 4th ed.

385
00:47:15,456 --> 00:47:19,381
New York, NY: McGraw Hill; 2020.

386
00:47:19,381 --> 00:47:23,744
With early diagnosis, medical management may be considered.

387
00:47:23,744 --> 00:47:29,994
However, consensus regarding MTX regimens is lacking because of small study numbers.

388
00:47:29,994 --> 00:47:40,756
Jermy and coworkers (2004) reported a 94-percent success with systemic MTX using a dose of 50 mg/m2 × BSA.

389
00:47:40,756 --> 00:47:44,906
Others employ a traditional multidose MTX regimen .

390
00:47:44,906 --> 00:47:50,906
Direct MTX injection into the gestational sac also offers comparable success .

391
00:47:50,906 --> 00:48:00,294
Last, a uterine artery MTX infusion followed by uterine artery embolization (UAE) is termed chemoembolization by some.

392
00:48:00,294 --> 00:48:04,331
This combined with systemic MTX has shown promise .

393
00:48:04,331 --> 00:48:11,556
The risk of uterine rupture with subsequent pregnancies following either medical or surgical management is undefined.

394
00:48:11,556 --> 00:48:21,719
Thus, elective cesarean delivery after 370/7 weeks’ gestation, which is timed similarly to those with prior at-risk myomectomy, is reasonable .

395
00:48:21,719 --> 00:48:32,069
Distinct from interstitial pregnancy, the term angular pregnancy is used by some to describe eccentric implantation near one cornu but within the endometrial cavity.

396
00:48:32,069 --> 00:48:42,694
In one prospective case series of 42 such pregnancies, 80 percent progressed to a viable age, and abnormal placentation or uterine rupture did not develop .

397
00:48:42,694 --> 00:48:49,169
These eccentrically implanted early IUPs are managed as normal pregnancies at our institution.

398
00:48:49,169 --> 00:48:51,794
Cesarean Scar Pregnancy.

399
00:48:51,794 --> 00:48:54,194
# Diagnosis.

400
00:48:54,194 --> 00:49:00,369
This term describes implantation within the myometrium of a prior cesarean delivery scar.

401
00:49:00,369 --> 00:49:08,069
Its incidence approximates 1 case in 2000 normal pregnancies and has increased along with the cesarean delivery rate .

402
00:49:08,069 --> 00:49:16,006
Women with symptomatic cesarean scar pregnancy (CSP) usually present early, and pain and bleeding are common.

403
00:49:16,006 --> 00:49:24,094
Still, up to 40 percent of women are asymptomatic, and the diagnosis is made during routine sonographic examination .

404
00:49:24,094 --> 00:49:28,631
Sonographic criteria are described in Figure 128 .

405
00:49:28,631 --> 00:49:34,944
Further, CSP implantation can be divided into endogenic and exogenic patterns.

406
00:49:34,944 --> 00:49:46,594
Endogenic CSPs implant on the scar and expand toward the uterine cavity, whereas exogenic ones implant deeply within the scar niche and grow toward the bladder or abdominal cavity.

407
00:49:46,594 --> 00:49:58,756
In one small study of CSPs that continued to viability, endogenic CSPs yielded variable obstetric outcomes, whereas all exogenic CSPs underwent hysterectomy

408
00:49:58,924 --> 00:50:03,174
with placenta accreta spectrum (PAS) at delivery .

409
00:50:03,124 --> 00:50:05,224
Figure 12-8.

410
00:50:05,224 --> 00:50:11,236
Transvaginal sonogram of a uterus with a cesarean scar pregnancy in a sagittal plane.

411
00:50:11,236 --> 00:50:32,849
Diagnostic criteria include: (1) an empty uterine cavity (E) and empty endocervical canal, (2) placenta or gestational sac (asterisk) embedded in the hysterotomy scar niche, (3) a thin myometrial mantle between the gestational sac and bladder (B), and (4) a prominent vascular pattern at the scar.

412
00:50:32,849 --> 00:50:37,361
C = cervix; Ut = anterior uterine wall.

413
00:50:37,361 --> 00:50:45,624
Sonographically, differentiating between an IUP implanted at the cervicoisthmic junction and a CSP can be difficult.

414
00:50:45,624 --> 00:50:52,874
Investigators in one study marked the midpoint of the uterine length (cervix to fundus) in sagittal views.

415
00:50:52,874 --> 00:50:59,049
If the center of the gestational sac lay distal to this midpoint, a CSP was diagnosed .

416
00:50:59,049 --> 00:51:02,811
A spontaneous expelling abortus is another mimic.

417
00:51:02,811 --> 00:51:10,636
Color Doppler will show the intense placental vascularity around a CSP, whereas as the aborting sac is avascular.

418
00:51:10,636 --> 00:51:19,361
Moreover, gentle pressure applied to the cervix by the vaginal probe will fail to move an implanted gestation—a negative sliding sign.

419
00:51:19,361 --> 00:51:24,211
Instead, an aborted sac will slide against the endocervical canal .

420
00:51:24,211 --> 00:51:31,499
TVS is the typical first-line imaging tool, but MR imaging is useful for inconclusive cases.

421
00:51:31,499 --> 00:51:33,724
# Management.

422
00:51:33,724 --> 00:51:39,174
Insights into the pathogenesis of CSPs are expanding management options.

423
00:51:39,174 --> 00:51:48,011
Namely, growing evidence suggests that some of these pregnancies will not behave as a typical ectopic pregnancy, and rupture rates are lower.

424
00:51:48,011 --> 00:51:52,099
CSPs are thought by some to be a precursor of PAS .

425
00:51:52,099 --> 00:52:05,699
As such, a significant percentage of affected pregnancies will progress to a viable-aged neonate, albeit with the complications associated with PAS (Calì, 2018; Timor-Tritsch, 2015b).

426
00:52:05,699 --> 00:52:11,611
Patients may prefer to avoid rupture and PAS risks and seek pregnancy termination.

427
00:52:11,611 --> 00:52:39,774
From one literature review, the most successful operations include: (1) laparoscopic uterine isthmic resection; (2) transvaginal isthmic resection through an anterior colpotomy, created similarly to anterior entry during vaginal hysterectomy; (3) UAE, followed by D & C with or without hysteroscopy; and (4) hysteroscopic resection (Birch Petersen, 2016; Wang, 2014).

428
00:52:39,774 --> 00:52:51,074
The Society for Maternal-Fetal Medicine (SMFM) (2020) considers sonography-guided vacuum aspiration alone, but not sharp curettage, to be suitable.

429
00:52:51,074 --> 00:52:58,036
In some instances, hysterectomy is required or may be elected in those not desiring future fertility.

430
00:52:58,036 --> 00:53:02,611
Medical management is an option for those hoping to avoid surgery.

431
00:53:02,611 --> 00:53:08,786
However, compared with surgery, pregnancy resolution rates are more varied and lengthier.

432
00:53:08,786 --> 00:53:20,899
In one review, local MTX injection into the gestational sac alone provided a success rate of 60 percent, and systemic plus local MTX raised the rate to nearly 80 percent .

433
00:53:20,899 --> 00:53:26,524
The SMFM (2020) recommends against systemic MTX alone.

434
00:53:26,524 --> 00:53:33,574
With local MTX, doses of 1 mg/kg or 50-mg doses have been described.

435
00:53:33,574 --> 00:53:43,124
Prior to local MTX, fetal death can be induced in more advanced gestations by potassium chloride (KCL) injection into the sac .

436
00:53:43,124 --> 00:53:48,299
One option is 1 mL of 2 mEq/mL KCL.

437
00:53:48,299 --> 00:53:55,799
Also, if associated bleeding complicates medical management, a Foley balloon catheter can be placed and expanded .

438
00:53:55,799 --> 00:54:04,524
Recently, a novel double-balloon catheter, in which the balloons lie in tandem, has been used with MTX to resolve CSPs .

439
00:54:04,524 --> 00:54:10,311
The cephalad balloon is filled within the endometrial cavity to prevent device expulsion.

440
00:54:10,311 --> 00:54:17,636
The lower balloon is tightly inflated to interrupt the CSP via mechanical pressure and tamponades potential bleeding.

441
00:54:17,636 --> 00:54:29,436
Following conservative treatment, subsequent pregnancies have good outcomes, but PAS and recurrent CSP are risks (Gao, 2016; Wang, 2015).

442
00:54:29,436 --> 00:54:37,611
In one series of 30 CSPs, five subsequent pregnancies developed normally, whereas four were recurrent CSPs .

443
00:54:37,611 --> 00:54:43,061
Uterine arteriovenous malformations are a potential long-term complication .

444
00:54:43,061 --> 00:54:46,711
CSPs have also been expectantly managed.

445
00:54:46,711 --> 00:54:52,886
The Society for Maternal– Fetal Medicine (2020) recommends against this practice.

446
00:54:52,886 --> 00:54:57,786
Exceptions may be early CSPs with evidence of pregnancy failure.

447
00:54:57,786 --> 00:55:03,774
One review of 69 patients continuing their gestation found that uterine rupture or

448
00:55:03,940 --> 00:55:09,577
dehiscence complicated 10 percent of all cases (Calì, 2018).

449
00:55:09,527 --> 00:55:15,390
During the first or second trimester, hysterectomy was performed in 15 percent.

450
00:55:15,390 --> 00:55:27,277
For the 40 patients progressing to the third trimester, 17 had placenta percreta, 23 patients underwent hysterectomy, and two patients had uterine rupture or dehiscence.

451
00:55:27,277 --> 00:55:33,002
For all trimesters, 60 percent of cases ultimately underwent hysterectomy.

452
00:55:33,002 --> 00:55:44,752
More reassuringly, in early pregnancies without cardiac activity, 70 percent had uncomplicated miscarriage, whereas 30 percent required surgical or medical intervention.

453
00:55:44,752 --> 00:55:48,765
Of these early demises, none required hysterectomy.

454
00:55:48,765 --> 00:55:55,215
Women accepting expectant care are ideally well counseled on these potential obstetric complications.

455
00:55:55,215 --> 00:56:10,715
If not prompted by earlier complications, repeat cesarean delivery is recommended at 340/7 and 356/7 weeks’ gestation, and this timing recognizes the PAS and uterine rupture risks associated with CSP.

456
00:56:10,715 --> 00:56:15,790
Betamethasone to hasten lung maturity is recommended prior to delivery .

457
00:56:15,790 --> 00:56:17,990
Cervical Pregnancy.

458
00:56:17,990 --> 00:56:20,390
# Diagnosis.

459
00:56:20,390 --> 00:56:28,365
This rare ectopic pregnancy is defined first by cervical glands noted histologically opposite the placental attachment site.

460
00:56:28,365 --> 00:56:37,677
Second, all or part of the placenta lies at a level below the entrance of the uterine vessels or below the peritoneal reflection on the anterior uterus.

461
00:56:37,677 --> 00:56:43,827
Trophoblast invades the endocervix, and the pregnancy develops in the fibrous cervical wall.

462
00:56:43,827 --> 00:56:48,140
Risk factors include ART and prior uterine curettage .

463
00:56:48,140 --> 00:56:55,090
Painless vaginal bleeding is reported by 90 percent of women with a cervical pregnancy, and it can be severe .

464
00:56:55,090 --> 00:57:02,665
As pregnancy progresses, a distended, thin-walled cervix with a partially dilated external os may be evident.

465
00:57:02,665 --> 00:57:07,740
Above the cervical mass, a slightly enlarged uterine fundus is felt.

466
00:57:07,740 --> 00:57:13,102
Typical sonographic findings are shown and described in Figure 12-9.

467
00:57:13,102 --> 00:57:18,615
In some cases, MR imaging and 3-D TVS can aid diagnosis.

468
00:57:18,615 --> 00:57:20,940
Figure 12-9.

469
00:57:20,940 --> 00:57:23,140
Cervical pregnancy.

470
00:57:23,140 --> 00:57:44,327
Transvaginal sonographic findings may include: (1) an hourglass uterine shape and ballooned cervix; (2) gestational tissue at the level of the cervix (arrow); (3) absent intrauterine gestational tissue; and (4) a portion of the endocervical canal seen interposed between the gestation and the endometrial canal.

471
00:57:44,327 --> 00:57:48,240
Reproduced with permission from Dr. Angela Seasely.

472
00:57:48,240 --> 00:57:54,377
At times, cervical ectopic pregnancy can mimic a miscarriage in transit through the cervix.

473
00:57:54,377 --> 00:58:09,965
Similar to CSPs and described in that section, color Doppler will show the intense vascularity of cervical implantation, and gentle pressure applied to the cervix by the vaginal probe will fail to move an implanted gestation—a negative sliding sign.

474
00:58:09,965 --> 00:58:12,190
# Management.

475
00:58:12,190 --> 00:58:16,240
Cervical pregnancy may be treated medically or surgically.

476
00:58:16,240 --> 00:58:23,340
In many centers, including ours, MTX is first-line therapy in hemodynamically stable women.

477
00:58:23,340 --> 00:58:30,365
Of options, single- or multidose systemic MTX and dosing found in Table 12-1 are suitable .

478
00:58:30,365 --> 00:58:41,140
Alternatively, 50 mg of MTX can be injected directly into the gestational sac (Jeng, 2007; Yamaguchi, 2017).

479
00:58:41,140 --> 00:58:49,802
Others describe chemoembolization with MTX and UAE, as described for interstitial pregnancy (p. 228).

480
00:58:49,802 --> 00:58:58,927
With MTX regimens, resolution and uterine preservation are achieved for gestations <12 weeks in 91 percent of cases .

481
00:58:58,927 --> 00:59:18,815
To select appropriate candidates, Hung and colleagues (1996) noted higher risks of systemic MTX treatment failure in those with a gestational age >9 weeks, βhCG levels >10,000 mIU/mL, crown-rump length >10 mm, and fetal cardiac activity.

482
00:59:18,815 --> 00:59:25,027
For this reason, feticidal KCL can be injected into the fetus or gestational sac .

483
00:59:25,027 --> 00:59:33,365
Notably, during posttherapy surveillance, sonographic resolution lags far behind serum β-hCG level regression .

484
00:59:33,365 --> 00:59:42,190
Although conservative management is feasible for many women with cervical pregnancies, suction evacuation or hysterectomy may be selected.

485
00:59:42,190 --> 00:59:48,252
Moreover, hysterectomy may be required with bleeding uncontrolled by conservative methods .

486
00:59:48,252 --> 00:59:57,077
During hysterectomy, because of the close proximity of the ureters to the ballooned cervix, urinary tract injury rates are a concern.

487
00:59:57,077 --> 01:00:03,190
If suction evacuation of the cervix is planned, intraoperative bleeding may be lessened by

488
01:00:03,340 --> 01:00:18,702
preoperative UAE, by intracervical vasopressin injection, or by a cerclage placed at the internal cervical os to compress feeding vessels (Chen, 2015; Fylstra, 2014; Wang, 2011).

489
01:00:18,652 --> 01:00:29,477
Cervical branches of the uterine artery can effectively be ligated with vaginal placement of hemostatic cervical sutures on the lateral aspects of the cervix at 3 and 9 o’clock .

490
01:00:29,477 --> 01:00:42,727
As an adjunct to medical or surgical therapy, UAE has been described either as a response to bleeding or as a preprocedural prevention (Hirakawa, 2009; Zakaria, 2011).

491
01:00:42,727 --> 01:00:55,652
Also, in the event of hemorrhage, a 26F Foley catheter with a 30-mL balloon can be placed intracervically and inflated to effect hemostasis by vessel tamponade and to monitor bloody drainage.

492
01:00:55,652 --> 01:01:02,552
The balloon remains inflated for 24 to 48 hours and is gradually decompressed over a few days .

493
01:01:02,552 --> 01:01:04,827
Abdominal Pregnancy.

494
01:01:04,827 --> 01:01:07,227
# Diagnosis.

495
01:01:07,227 --> 01:01:17,352
These rare ectopic pregnancies are defined as an implantation in the peritoneal cavity exclusive of tubal, ovarian, or intraligamentous implantations.

496
01:01:17,352 --> 01:01:22,902
Most are thought to follow early tubal rupture or tubal abortion with reimplantation.

497
01:01:22,902 --> 01:01:26,452
Clinically, symptoms may be absent or vague.

498
01:01:26,452 --> 01:01:33,752
Laboratory tests are typically uninformative, although maternal serum alpha-fetoprotein levels can be elevated.

499
01:01:33,752 --> 01:01:40,365
With later gestations, abnormal fetal positions may be palpated, or the cervix is displaced .

500
01:01:40,365 --> 01:01:59,940
Sonographically, clues are a fetus or placenta seen eccentrically positioned within the pelvis or separate from the uterus; lack of myometrium between the fetus and the maternal anterior abdominal wall or bladder; or bowel loops surrounding the gestational sac (Allibone, 1981; Chukus, 2015).

501
01:01:59,940 --> 01:02:03,727
Oligohydramnios is common but nonspecific.

502
01:02:03,727 --> 01:02:09,590
Often needed, MR imaging can aid diagnosis and provide placental information.

503
01:02:09,590 --> 01:02:11,815
# Management.

504
01:02:11,815 --> 01:02:16,990
Abdominal pregnancy treatment depends on the gestational age at diagnosis.

505
01:02:16,990 --> 01:02:22,940
Conservative expectant management carries a maternal risk for sudden, dangerous hemorrhage.

506
01:02:22,940 --> 01:02:30,515
Moreover, Stevens (1993) reported fetal malformations and deformations in 20 percent.

507
01:02:30,515 --> 01:02:36,477
Thus, we believe that termination generally is indicated once the diagnosis is made.

508
01:02:36,477 --> 01:02:42,727
Certainly, before 24 weeks’ gestation, conservative treatment rarely is justified.

509
01:02:42,727 --> 01:02:48,227
Despite this, some describe waiting until fetal viability with close surveillance .

510
01:02:48,227 --> 01:02:56,177
Principal surgical objectives are delivery of the fetus and careful assessment of placental implantation without provoking hemorrhage.

511
01:02:56,177 --> 01:03:04,115
Unnecessary exploration is avoided because the anatomy is commonly distorted and surrounding areas are extremely vascular.

512
01:03:04,115 --> 01:03:15,490
Importantly, placental removal may precipitate torrential hemorrhage because the normal hemostatic mechanism of myometrial contraction to constrict hypertrophied blood vessels is lacking.

513
01:03:15,490 --> 01:03:23,940
If it is obvious that the placenta can be safely removed or if the implantation site is already bleeding, then removal begins immediately.

514
01:03:23,940 --> 01:03:28,402
Blood vessels supplying the placenta are ideally ligated first.

515
01:03:28,402 --> 01:03:34,152
For early gestations, locally injected dilute vasopressin also can be employed.

516
01:03:34,152 --> 01:03:38,840
Some advocate leaving the placenta in place as the lesser of two evils.

517
01:03:38,840 --> 01:03:45,152
It decreases the chance of immediate life-threatening hemorrhage, but at the expense of long-term sequelae.

518
01:03:45,152 --> 01:03:54,752
Placental embolization may play a role prior to or following fetal extraction (Frischhertz, 2019; Marcelin, 2018).

519
01:03:54,752 --> 01:04:07,715
If left in the abdominal cavity, the placenta can form abscesses, adhesions, intestinal or ureteral obstruction, and wound dehiscence (Bergstrom, 1998; Martin, 1988).

520
01:04:07,715 --> 01:04:12,140
In many of these cases, surgical removal becomes inevitable.

521
01:04:12,140 --> 01:04:24,677
If the placenta is left, its involution can be monitored using serum β-hCG levels and color Doppler sonography or MR imaging (France, 1980; Martin, 1990).

522
01:04:24,677 --> 01:04:28,215
Placental function usually declines rapidly.

523
01:04:28,215 --> 01:04:34,615
The placenta is eventually resorbed, but this can take months or years with advanced gestations .

524
01:04:34,615 --> 01:04:40,527
If the placenta is left, postoperative MTX is often given to hasten involution.

525
01:04:40,527 --> 01:04:45,990
Accelerated placental destruction with accumulation of necrotic tissue follows .

526
01:04:45,990 --> 01:04:50,065
Infection with abscess formation can be a complication .

527
01:04:50,065 --> 01:04:53,965
Similar to persistent trophoblastic tissue, early

528
01:04:54,124 --> 01:04:56,924
gestations may benefit most .

529
01:04:56,874 --> 01:04:59,149
Ovarian Pregnancy.

530
01:04:59,149 --> 01:05:06,661
Ectopic implantation of the fertilized egg in the ovary is rare and is diagnosed if four clinical criteria are met.

531
01:05:06,661 --> 01:05:28,711
These were outlined by Spiegelberg (1878): (1) the ipsilateral tube is intact and distinct from the ovary; (2) the ectopic pregnancy occupies the ovary; (3) the ectopic pregnancy is connected by the uteroovarian ligament to the uterus; and (4) ovarian tissue can be demonstrated histologically amid the placental tissue.

532
01:05:28,711 --> 01:05:35,561
Risk factors are similar to those for tubal pregnancies, but ART or IUD failure are prominent .

533
01:05:35,561 --> 01:05:40,661
Presenting complaints and findings mirror those for tubal ectopic pregnancy.

534
01:05:40,661 --> 01:05:49,799
Although the ovary can accommodate the expanding pregnancy more easily than the fallopian tube, rupture at an early stage is the usual consequence .

535
01:05:49,799 --> 01:05:58,836
Sonographically, an internal anechoic area is surrounded by a wide echogenic ring, which in turn is surrounded by ovarian cortex .

536
01:05:58,836 --> 01:06:08,324
In one review of 49 cases, the diagnosis was not be made until surgery, and many cases were presumed to be a tubal ectopic pregnancy .

537
01:06:08,324 --> 01:06:17,374
Moreover, at surgery, an early, unrecognized ovarian pregnancy may instead be considered and managed as a hemorrhagic corpus luteum.

538
01:06:17,374 --> 01:06:21,574
Evidence-based management accrues mainly from case reports .

539
01:06:21,574 --> 01:06:26,286
Classically, management for ovarian pregnancies has been surgical.

540
01:06:26,286 --> 01:06:34,849
Selection of laparoscopy or laparotomy are influenced by gestational age, hemoperitoneum, and hemodynamic status.

541
01:06:34,849 --> 01:06:46,774
Small lesions can be managed by ovarian wedge resection or cystectomy, whereas larger lesions require oophorectomy (Elwell, 2015; Melcer, 2015).

542
01:06:46,774 --> 01:06:53,499
With conservative surgery, βhCG levels should be monitored to exclude remnant trophoblast.

543
01:06:53,499 --> 01:06:55,924
Heterotopic Pregnancy.

544
01:06:55,924 --> 01:07:05,636
This pairing of an IUP and an ectopically located pregnancy is rare, and the most common dyad is an IUP and an ampullary tubal pregnancy.

545
01:07:05,636 --> 01:07:12,536
The natural incidence of these heterotopic pregnancies approximates 1 case per 30,000 pregnancies .

546
01:07:12,536 --> 01:07:18,849
However, with ART, their incidence is higher and is 9 cases in 10,000 pregnancies .

547
01:07:18,849 --> 01:07:23,311
Initial clinical symptoms usually reflect those from the ectopic.

548
01:07:23,311 --> 01:07:32,674
Because an IUP is seen sonographically and the ectopic pregnancy may not be visualized, rates of rupture are higher in heterotopic pregnancy .

549
01:07:32,674 --> 01:07:38,786
In patients wishing to preserve the IUP, management initially is dictated by bleeding.

550
01:07:38,786 --> 01:07:43,586
In those with hemorrhage, treatment of the ectopic pregnancy is surgical.

551
01:07:43,586 --> 01:07:49,986
Depending on the ectopic location, resection or suction aspiration is the most common method .

552
01:07:49,986 --> 01:07:58,249
Of note, adjunctive UAE and vasopressin and their effects on uterine blood flow are less desirable for the ongoing IUP.

553
01:07:58,249 --> 01:08:06,436
With a rare comorbid ovarian ectopic pregnancy, early excision of the corpus luteum merits progesterone supplementation .

554
01:08:06,436 --> 01:08:17,336
In those without significant bleeding, medical steps to disrupt the ectopic pregnancy typically involve gestational-sac injection of KCl or of hyperosmolar glucose.

555
01:08:17,336 --> 01:08:22,824
This may be followed by later aspiration evacuation of the ectopic gestation.

556
01:08:22,824 --> 01:08:27,261
Because of toxicity to the IUP, MTX is avoided.

557
01:08:27,261 --> 01:08:33,436
With ongoing pregnancy, adverse neonatal outcome rates are not appreciably elevated .

558
01:08:33,436 --> 01:08:38,649
However, initial sonographic surveillance of fetal growth seems reasonable.

559
01:08:38,649 --> 01:08:49,611
Route of ultimate delivery is influenced mainly by myometrial integrity following ectopic treatment (Dendas, 2017; OuYang, 2014).

